# Diction - forty-four singers and an Init, for the built-in voice or a recorded one.
#
# A patch is a singer: the size of the throat, how hard and how rough it
# sings, how it moves between notes, and how many sing. The voice itself is
# the track's, so every patch here has to sound like itself in the built-in
# voice and in anybody's recorded one. The knobs only a recorded voice has
# (clean, source, throat) are an extra in a few, never the whole of one.
#
# The throat is `formant`. Down is bigger and darker, up smaller and
# brighter, and it doesn't move the pitch. Play a patch low or high for a low
# or high singer: the notes decide that.
#
# Families: voices, colour, style, choir, harmony, strange. The harmony
# family sings a chord on every note; it's auditioned on chords.
#
# Every patch but Init carries eight named macros. Destinations are numbered
# as in Diction.h's MacroDest: #1 vowel, #2 formant, #3 breath,
# #4 consonants, #5 vibrato, #6 vibrato rate, #7 vibrato delay, #8 drift,
# #9 glide, #10 attack, #11 release, #12 velocity, #13 volume,
# #14 consonant level, #15 clean, #16 effort, #17 rasp, #18 growl,
# #19 whisper, #20 scoop, #21 track, #22 spread, #23 source, #24 throat,
# #25 morph, #26 pitch (24 semitones a unit). Each family has its own set of
# eight, all of them ones the built-in voice can be heard to do. A macro
# whose knob has no room left goes the other way under the opposite name
# (Smaller, Straight, Voiced...). Where a macro at full moves the level by
# more than 1 dB, a volume route takes it back out.

machine Diction

patch Init family=voices

patch Deep family=voices
  # A big, dark throat, sung a little soft. Best low.
  formant        -6 st
  effort         -0.2
  vibrato        22 ct
  vibratorate    5 Hz
  set macro1 "Bigger"
  mac1_d1  #2
  mac1_a1  -0.25
  set macro2 "Belt"
  mac2_d1  #16
  mac2_a1  0.4
  mac2_d2  #13
  mac2_a2  -0.115
  set macro3 "Air"
  mac3_d1  #3
  mac3_a1  0.4
  set macro4 "Vibrato"
  mac4_d1  #5
  mac4_a1  0.35
  mac4_d2  #7
  mac4_a2  -0.1
  set macro5 "Brighter"
  mac5_d1  #1
  mac5_a1  0.3
  set macro6 "Wander"
  mac6_d1  #8
  mac6_a1  0.4
  set macro7 "Slower"
  mac7_d1  #10
  mac7_a1  0.25
  mac7_d2  #11
  mac7_a2  0.15
  set macro8 "Octave Down"
  mac8_d1  #26
  mac8_a1  -0.5

